## 2 NFRs Chosen 
QR01 - The system should have an interface that trained users can feel comfortable using and accessing 
QR02 - The system should allow Volunteers to view all of their information that is being stored, 
and allow them to opt out of certain information being held if they feel is not needed

## Why do they matter? 
These NFRs matter so that the System can be useable by it's intended users efficiently without causing mass issue
and also to ensure that the data is kept and hekd responsibly as needed to comply with GDPR Regulations 

## Must, Should, or Could? 
QR01 - Should, while the system would still work without the training of the users, it would be much less efficient and cause
long term issue if left untested and unchecked 

QR02 - Must, Due to the regulations of the GDPR, Any stored data if a user must be available within one month of making a data access request 

